<title>UK: Credit Lyonnais sets warrants on German stocks.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais sets warrants on German stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais Financial Products, Guernsey, has issued five million European-style bull and bear range warrants in ten equal tranches, on Allianz, Deutsche Bank, Dresdner Bank, Daimler and Siemens lead manager BfG Bank AG, Frankfurt said.</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p>ONE WARRANT CONTROLS ONE SHARE.</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	02.JUL.97		 PAYDATE	25.SEP.96</p>
<p> LISTING	   FRANKFURT		 MIN EXER LOT 100</p>
<p>* * * * * * * * *</p>
<p>WARRANT	    SPOT	RANGE	   ISSUE</p>
<p>ALLIANZ	   2660 DEM</p>
<p>BULL			    2600-2900	6.11 DEM</p>
<p>BEAR			    2700-2450	5.80 DEM</p>
<p>DEUTSCHE BANK   71.5 DEM</p>
<p>BULL			    70.0-76.0	5.80 DEM</p>
<p>BEAR			    74.0-68.0	5.95 DEM</p>
<p>DRESDNER BANK   40.9 DEM</p>
<p>BULL			    39.5-42.5	5.80 DEM</p>
<p>BEAR			    41.5-38.5	5.45 DEM</p>
<p>DAIMLER	   81.0 DEM</p>
<p>BULL			    79.0-86.0	5.95 DEM</p>
<p>BEAR			    82.0-75.0	5.55 DEM</p>
<p>SIEMENS	   78.0 DEM</p>
<p>BULL			    77.0-84.0	5.90 DEM</p>
<p>BEAR			    79.0-72.0	5.95 DEM</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
